{"id":"trans-dinarica-bike","title":"Trans Dinarica by bike: Ljubljana to Kotor","who":"Classic route · the Western Balkans' new cycling trail","when":"May–June and September–October","vehicle":"Gravel or touring bike, 3–4 weeks","kind":"bike","color":"#0e7490","summary":"A slice of the 2024 Trans Dinarica cycling route across eight countries: from Ljubljana through Slovenia's karst and Croatia's Plitvice lakes, the Bosnian highlands, Sarajevo and Mostar's bridge, to the fjord-like Bay of Kotor. Gravel, quiet asphalt, no signposts yet: use the official route data.","sources":[{"label":"Epic Road Rides: Trans Dinarica in Slovenia (July 2025)","url":"https://epicroadrides.com/cycling-blog/trans-dinarica-bike-touring-in-slovenia/"},{"label":"Rouleur: making a 3,364 km route across eight countries","url":"https://rouleur.cc/blogs/rouleur-explore/what-goes-into-making-a-3-364km-cycle-route-across-eight-countries"}],"approximate":"Main towns; the route is not signposted and the line is a guide only.","km":992,"bbox":[14.1545,42.4221,18.7713,46.0501],"stops":[{"name":"Ljubljana","place":"Ljubljana, Slovenia","at":[46.05,14.5069],"text":"Slovenia's green little capital.","photo":{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c7/Ljubljana_Old_Town%2C_Slovenia_%28Old_Camera%29_%2833286165680%29.jpg/500px-Ljubljana_Old_Town%2C_Slovenia_%28Old_Camera%29_%2833286165680%29.jpg","page":"Ljubljana","source":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Ljubljana_Old_Town%2C_Slovenia_%28Old_Camera%29_%2833286165680%29.jpg","credit":"Andrew Milligan Sumo","license":"CC BY 2.0"}},{"name":"Postojna","place":"Postojna, Slovenia","at":[45.7873,14.1593],"text":"Karst caves and forests.","source":{"label":"Epic Road Rides (2025)","url":"https://epicroadrides.com/cycling-blog/trans-dinarica-bike-touring-in-slovenia/"},"photo":{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/74/Postojna_%2822206343750%29.jpg/500px-Postojna_%2822206343750%29.jpg","page":"Postojna Cave